        "## 11. PCA Visualization\n",
        "\n",
        "Principal Component Analysis (PCA) is used to reduce the three-dimensional feature space into two principal components for visualization while preserving as much variance as possible."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SqlhNvStgKff"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
        "\n",
        "pca = PCA(n_components=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "X_pca = pca.fit_transform(X_scaled)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
